r": "vishwajeet.ssj", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17991413546863490, "text": "Those are her best years of her life. Even tho she will look at those videos with disgust and cringe for herself in the future.", "created_at": "2025-12-07T13:33:55", "owner": "__ulen__", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17865504555518593, "text": "Three months later she’s asking why you haven’t noticed her new nails.", "created_at": "2025-12-07T12:50:17", "owner": "grittymeats", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18111122692716588, "text": "Someone’s future mother, someone’s future father, someone’s future husband and someone’s future wife, someone’s daughter and someone’s son\nBoth are embarrassing", "created_at": "2025-12-07T08:44:37", "owner": "nobid_leon", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17882354859422122, "text": "", "created_at": "2025-12-07T05:00:45", "owner": "ky404_", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18103564687678497, "text": "Pobres padres, tener una hija para acabar asi de puta", "created_at": "2025-12-07T04:47:41", "owner": "sergio_losmiios", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18033726158721882, "text": "Ngl if you see boobs and immediately think of her father, you might be gay..??", "created_at": "2025-12-07T04:15:42", "owner": "__3velynn7", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17956247105974889, "text": "The Pythagorean theorem states that in a right-angled triangle, the square of the hypotenuse (the side opposite the right angle, 'c') is equal to the sum of the squares of the other two sides ('a' and 'b'), expressed as a² + b² = c². This formula allows you to find the length of any side if you know the other two, and it also works in reverse to determine if a triangle is a right triangle. \nHow it works\nIdentify the sides: In a right triangle, 'a' and 'b' are the two shorter sides (legs) that form the 90° angle, and 'c' is the longest side (hypotenuse). \nThe formula: a² + b² = c². \nTo find the hypotenuse (c): If you know 'a' and 'b', you square them, add the results, and then take the square root of the sum. \nExample: For a triangle with sides 3 and 4, c² = 3² + 4² = 9 + 16 = 25. So, c = √25 = 5. \nTo find a leg (a or b): If you know the hypotenuse and one leg, you rearrange the formula (e.g., a² = c² - b²) and solve. \nExample: For a triangle with hypotenuse 15 and leg 9, b² = 15² - 9² = 225 - 81 = 144. So, b = √144 = 12. \nKey takeaway\nThe theorem only applies to right-angled triangles.\nIt's a fundamental concept in geometry with many practical applications.", "created_at": "2025-12-07T03:48:19", "owner": "14_gobbilitty", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17892733710374562, "text": "Angle ❌️ angel✅️", "created_at": "2025-12-07T03:08:22", "owner": "vincent____5_11____", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17963851593006782, "text": "😍", "created_at": "2025-12-07T02:48:25", "owner": "notyour_sanjanaa", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18083432381024395, "text": "", "created_at": "2025-12-07T02:48:20", "owner": "crowbarhit", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18066319412431878, "text": "🤢🤢🤢", "created_at": "2025-12-07T00:05:01", "owner": "_loqui_stvz_", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17897679975204795, "text": "Thatd why she's single", "created_at": "2025-12-06T22:38:49", "owner": "_kyeongkcmorris.__", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18087687250969517, "text": "Someones daughter, possibly sibling, and future wife", "created_at": "2025-12-06T21:59:14", "owner": "sr.71.black.bird", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18091260992505255, "text": "That's so me 😂", "created_at": "2025-12-06T21:47:06", "owner": "sx_tanuu", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18031595705735200, "text": "+91 95129 70707", "created_at": "2025-12-06T21:46:40", "owner": "krishaaa.211", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18070286984367077, "text": "Yeah she needs a shower", "created_at": "2025-12-06T21:00:25", "owner": "nate.peed", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18106965412730312, "text": "🐄", "created_at": "2025-12-06T20:30:44", "owner": "alemassuer", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18092053519921199, "text": "Fatherless behavior", "created_at": "2025-12-06T20:09:28", "owner": "aj_sandiego07", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17916863697231113, "text": "Angel*", "created_at": "2025-12-06T19:47:01", "owner": "